.env

# `data/*`, not `data/` -- a bare `data/` makes git treat the whole tree as
# an excluded directory it never descends into, so no negation below it can
# ever re-include anything (confirmed live: `!data/outputs/**` had no effect
# at all under a bare `data/` ignore). `data/*` still ignores everything
# directly under data/ by default but leaves git willing to look inside.
#
# SPEC-ADDENDUM-05.md SS B.3: consensus projections are perishable and not
# re-fetchable after the week passes, unlike nflverse data -- the prediction
# log is committed to git despite the blanket data/ ignore. Each level below
# is re-ignored immediately after being opened, so this exposes only
# data/outputs/<league_slug>/prediction_log/ -- not the rest of data/outputs/
# (confirmed live: an earlier version of this chain that skipped the
# re-ignore steps accidentally exposed every other file under
# data/outputs/<league_slug>/, e.g. draft_board.csv).
data/*
!data/outputs/
data/outputs/*
!data/outputs/*/
data/outputs/*/*
!data/outputs/*/prediction_log/
!data/outputs/*/prediction_log/**
rankings/
vendor/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

/image.png

# Project docs/notes kept local-only, not shown on GitHub.
*.md
!README.md
docs/
